  "about": "Curated map labels (owner request 2026-10-13: names of the busiest buildings, UChicago dorms and prominent off-campus places the shuttles serve, shown by default like Google Maps). tools/build_landmarks.py resolves every entry to OpenStreetMap coordinates (osm = the exact OSM name in web/data/places.json, or an explicit OSM object for places outside it) and writes web/data/landmarks.json. Order = label priority within a tier (first wins a collision). tier 1 = shown from zoom 14.5 (the app opens at 15), 2 = from 16, 3 = from 17; until (optional) = hidden from that zoom on (a group name that splits into its buildings when you zoom in, like Max Palevsky). kind: library, hub, dorm, housing (off-campus apartments), dining, academic, medical, arts, sports, shop, transit, landmark. Edit this file, then run python tools/build_landmarks.py.",
